{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.WeakSymmetricNormalization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.WeakSymmetricNormalization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weak_symmetric_normalization_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weak_symmetric_normalization_eq","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/weak-symmetric-normalization.lean#L124-L133","doc":"Direct unfold of the definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weak_symmetric_normalization_factored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weak_symmetric_normalization_factored","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/weak-symmetric-normalization.lean#L113-L122","doc":"Algebraic-identity form: factor `q^4` out of the expression. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weak_symmetric_normalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weak_symmetric_normalization","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/weak-symmetric-normalization.lean#L95-L111","doc":"The symmetric-channel normalization in `R[1/3]`:\n\n  N_sym(q) := (q^4 + q^6 + q^8) / 3\n            = q^4 · (1 + q^2 + q^4) / 3\n            = q^4 · [3]_{q^2} / 3.\n\nRequires `R` to contain `1/3` (i.e. `Invertible (3 : R)`); this\nholds for the canonical specializations `R = ℚ(q)` and\n`R = ℚ[q, q⁻¹]`.\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:weak-symmetric-normalization","label":"prop:weak-symmetric-normalization","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/weak-symmetric-normalization.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeakSymmetricNormalization.link_triplet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeakSymmetricNormalization.link_triplet","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/weak-symmetric-normalization.lean#L93-L93","doc":"Upstream: `conj:electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet`\ndischarged for this `q` (W↔T(2,4), Z↔T(2,6), H↔T(2,8) on\nBring). Refined per audit\n2026-05-05-path-alpha-bring-refinement to drop\nhost-distinctness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeakSymmetricNormalization.spectral_completeness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeakSymmetricNormalization.spectral_completeness","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/weak-symmetric-normalization.lean#L87-L87","doc":"Upstream: `conj:weak-spectral-completeness` discharged for\nthis `q`. Encoded as a class hypothesis since the\nconjecture itself depends on U2 + U4 (currently open). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeakSymmetricNormalization.q_not_root_of_unity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeakSymmetricNormalization.q_not_root_of_unity","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/weak-symmetric-normalization.lean#L83-L83","doc":"Generic-q hypothesis: q is NOT a root of unity in R. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeakSymmetricNormalization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeakSymmetricNormalization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/weak-symmetric-normalization.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeakSymmetricNormalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WeakSymmetricNormalization","kind":"class","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/weak-symmetric-normalization.lean#L65-L93","doc":"A `WeakSymmetricNormalization R q` instance encodes:\n\n- `q` is generic in `R` (NOT a root of unity in `R`; q ≠ 1).\n- The two upstream conjectures\n  (`conj:weak-spectral-completeness` and\n  `conj:electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet`) hold for the\n  triplet `{T(2,4), T(2,6), T(2,8)}` on Bring's surface.\n\nThe closed-form expression\n  `N_sym(q) = (q^4 + q^6 + q^8) / 3 ∈ R[1/3]`\nis then a `def`, not a conjecture; it follows mechanically\nfrom the Wedderburn projector + Frobenius trace formulas.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWLinkTripletIdentified","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWLinkTripletIdentified","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/weak-symmetric-normalization.lean#L56-L63","doc":"Predicate: the EW link-triplet identification\nW ↔ T(2,4), Z ↔ T(2,6), H ↔ T(2,8) holds on Bring.\nConditional on `conj:electroweak-higgs-torus-link-triplet`\nbeing discharged (currently open: gated on U2 + U4).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWSpectralCompletenessHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.EWSpectralCompletenessHolds","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/weak-symmetric-normalization.lean#L42-L54","doc":"Predicate: the EW spectral-completeness conjecture holds for\nthe parameter `q`.  Conditional on `conj:weak-spectral-\ncompleteness` being discharged (currently open: gated on U2\n+ U4 + Hoefsmit cell-content correctness).  The categorical\ncontent is \"the eight pure-pattern projectors of σ_1, σ_3,\nσ_5 on V^⊗6 are pairwise orthogonal and exhaust the EW\nWedderburn content.\"\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsRootOfUnity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IsRootOfUnity","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/weak-symmetric-normalization.lean#L32-L40","doc":"Predicate: `q : R` is a root of unity in `R`.\n\nEncoded explicitly so that the generic-q hypothesis in\n`WeakSymmetricNormalization` is a propositional condition,\nnot a placeholder.\n","signatureChunk":0}]}